<CaseStudyLayout
  title="nuVector"
  description="I redesigned and rebuilt nuVector's company website on Astro, with services, client logos, case studies and a blog. The main call to action is a demo request."
  client="nuVector LLC (Atlanta, Georgia)"
  role="Design and front-end development"
  year="2024 to 2025"
  slides={[
    {
      title: 'Hero, services and clients',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-nuvector-intro.mp4',
      poster: '/images/nuvector-intro.webp',
    },
    {
      title: 'Platform, case studies and about',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-nuvector-platform.mp4',
      poster: '/images/nuvector-platform.webp',
    },
    {
      title: 'Blog and demo request',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-nuvector-blog.mp4',
      poster: '/images/nuvector-blog.webp',
    },
  ]}
  highlights={[
    { value: 'Built on Astro', label: 'Static pages with no plugins to maintain' },
    { value: 'Client logos', label: 'Volvo, ZF, Sonoco and others near the top of the page' },
    { value: 'One call to action', label: 'Request a demo, repeated through the page' },
  ]}
  overview={[
    'nuVector makes returnable asset management software for manufacturers and logistics teams. It tracks containers, racks and tooling that leave a plant and are supposed to come back. I worked there as a front-end developer and later in SEO and marketing, so I knew the customers. The company website had a different job from the <a class="text-link" href="/web-developer-project-loopmanager">LoopManager product site</a>. It needed to show that nuVector is an established company and get visitors to book a demo. I redesigned and rebuilt it with that in mind.',
    'The page opens with a short headline and a demo button. Below that are a services section (supply chain optimization, workflow tracking and data infrastructure), client logos including Volvo, Warner Bros. Discovery, Sonoco, Regal and ZF, a feature section, case studies, a short company history and the blog. The page ends with a full-width demo request section and a footer with contact details. The orange and charcoal brand colors and the nuVector logo mark are used throughout.',
    'The site is built on Astro as a static site, so pages load quickly and there is no plugin stack to maintain. The blog holds the SEO content, with posts on RFID readers, construction asset tracking and returnable asset trends. Each post targets a specific search and ends with a link to the demo form.',
    'Together with the LoopManager product site, this gave nuVector a consistent set of websites from company overview to product to demo request.',
  ]}
  tools={['Astro', 'HTML & CSS', 'JavaScript', 'TypeScript', 'Figma', 'SEO']}
/>
